  "purpose": "Line drawings that register on each homepage card cover (frame 0), for the \"Drawn, then built\" card arrival.",
  "renderer": "Three.js r185 project inspector (studio-inspector.js and its modules) from commit e42a05b49b44d563fb635b4994e68834ab6982fa, loaded as tools/white-studio/export.js loads a cover: 900x600 selection canvas, source camera reset, progress 0; AURA with its aura-reframe-20261022 framing. Tool: tools/card-lines/.",
  "method": "Two geometry passes at 4800x3200 (4x the 1200 w cover) store view normals, part ids and 24-bit view depth. Lines between neighbouring pixels: model outline and depth steps #111316; seams between parts and folds of at least crease_deg #505b66. Each line is centred on its boundary at line_px output pixels (line_px_small below 1200 w), box-averaged to each width. No cover pixel is read to draw the lines. Transparent background; lossless WebP of coverage stored in alpha_levels steps (near-lossless).",
  "registration": "The harness also re-encodes its own frame-0 render with the exporter settings (WebP q.94, 1800x1200). Byte-identical to the published cover: steering, brakeSim, scanner, javelin, materialTest, aura, seat, pool, lineFollower, formlabs, telecaster, education, ftc. Not byte-identical, same geometry and camera (zero phase-correlation shift; transmission or carbon-weave shading differs by at most 11 levels): vineRobot, carbonSeat.",
